  "term": "soft palate",
  "definition": "The soft palate is part of the oropharyngeal region and plays an important role in swallowing, breathing, hearing, and speech. In this source, it is also described as a structure whose development involves signaling pathways such as Wnt, Hh, and Fgf, especially during muscle formation.",
